*~
s3cfg
\#*\#
#
# intermediate / generated fiiles
#
#
# A script I use all over the place hard coded to what I am currently
# reviewing must be ignored
vp
renderall.sh
*.incl
*.errlog
*.stylelog
output.rtc
.claude/settings.local.json
# 2026-10-26 directory-naming retrofit: every course now names its pdfs
# directories uniformly as <prefix><unit-or-fc>-pdfs/ (afu1-pdfs/,
# cvu2-pdfs/, affc-pdfs/, cvfc-pdfs/, ...), so one depth-agnostic pattern
# covers all of them -- unit dirs and fc dirs alike -- instead of the two
# separate patterns this used to need. Deliberately not restricted to
# *.pdf: covers everything generated under any -pdfs/ directory (so a new
# generated-file type showing up here shouldn't require another line),
# matching the old fc-pdfs/ pattern's intent rather than the old, narrower
# lessons-pdfs/ one. Already-tracked */-pdfs/placeholder.txt files are
# unaffected: gitignore only hides untracked files, never untracks
# something already committed.
**/*-pdfs/*
dist/
dist/*
__pycache__/
__pycache__/*
build/
build/*
# images generated from each unit's -gp/-tableaux scripts so ignore them
# (every course now names its media directories uniformly as
# <prefix><unit-or-fc>-media/, e.g. afu1-media/, cvu2-media/, affc-media/;
# images is a local symlink alias to whichever one is active, see below).
**/*-media/*.png
# local rendering convenience symlink, recreated per work session
# (points at whichever unit's real *lessons-media dir you're working on),
# never committed. No trailing slash: a trailing-slash pattern only
# matches real directories, not symlinks, and images is always a symlink.
# '**/' (rather than a leading '/') since it now lives one level inside
# whichever course directory is active (2026-10-04), not the true repo root.
**/images
**/bucket/*
**/content/*
**/courses/*